{"$schema":"vscode://schemas/color-theme","_papyrus":{"direction":"Blueprint Ink (v3) — cool teal/green syntax with a violet accent on warm cream. A deliberate divergence from the warm Papyrus system (Vellum/Noir/Lamplight stay warm).","roles":{"keyword":"#2C5E64 deep teal-slate","function":"#157E6A teal","string":"#1E7A52 emerald","classType":"#2C6E8C blueprint blue","accent":"#4A38A0 violet (self/important only)","number":"#7A5418 brass","annotation":"#6A4A16 ochre","ink":"#13161A cool near-black","foreground":"#1F2428 cool slate"},"violetRule":"#4A38A0 is reserved for self/this and the single most-important token class. Never an everyday role — it is the one loud color.","variableWeight":"Identifiers read medium-weight (500) in the design studio. VS Code fontStyle supports only bold/italic, so the shipped theme keeps variables normal; users may set editor.fontWeight:500 globally to match.","ink":"Base ink #13161A is a cool near-black (faint blue cast) that reinforces the blueprint direction; two-tier with prose foreground #1F2428 (identifiers darker/heavier than prose).","contrast":"All content tokens deepened to >=4.5:1 on the #FCF6E6 cream (cool hues sit at the 600-700 band, not brighter, so they pass AA).","spec":"Full rationale in papyrus-inkwell-design-language.md. Single source of truth: papyrus-palettes.js."},"name":"Papyrus Inkwell","type":"light","colors":{"editor.background":"#FCF6E6","editor.foreground":"#1F2428","editor.lineHighlightBackground":"#F4EFDA","editor.selectionBackground":"#C8C0A075","editor.inactiveSelectionBackground":"#C8C0A040","editor.selectionHighlightBackground":"#C8C0A075","editor.wordHighlightBackground":"#C8C0A040","editor.wordHighlightStrongBackground":"#C8C0A075","editor.findMatchBackground":"#5C3A1F70","editor.findMatchHighlightBackground":"#5C3A1F30","editorLineNumber.foreground":"#A8A593","editorLineNumber.activeForeground":"#3A4148","editorCursor.foreground":"#1F2428","editorWhitespace.foreground":"#EBE4C8","editorIndentGuid